    "index": 1,
    "title": "The Database Lives on the Server",
    "from": "Maya, founder of NimbusCart",
    "brief": "We have 1,000 paying customers! Orders, accounts and stock all live in a database on the same server as the website. Dinner time is getting slow. Can you keep it fast without breaking the bank?",
    "lesson": "Vertical scaling (a bigger instance) is the quickest fix. But a database on the web server competes for CPU, and its data lives on a single disk. Read the post-mortem warnings.",
